\section{Conclusions}

In this work, we investigated budgeted example selection for annotation for ICL, a previously under-explored area. Seeking for an effective and efficient selection, we introduce \adaicl, a diversity-based uncertainty selection strategy. Diversity-based sampling improves effectiveness, while uncertainty sampling improves budget efficiency and helps the LLM learn new information about the task. 
Extensive experiments in low-resource settings show that \adaicl outperforms other approaches in five NLP tasks using seven different LLMs. Moreover, \adaicl can result into considerable budget savings, while it also needs fewer ICL examples during inference to achieve a given level of performance, reducing inference costs. Finally, our calibration analysis showed that \adaicl selects examples that lead to well-calibrated predictions.






