\subsection{Different notions of curvature}
\label{sec:exp-curv}
\noindent So far, we have implemented LCP with Ollivier-Ricci curvature in all experiments. However, other notions of curvature have been considered in Graph Machine Learning applications, including in rewiring. (\cite{fesser2023mitigating}) use the Augmented Forman-Ricci curvature (AFRC), which enriches the Forman-Ricci curvature (FRC) by considering 3-cycles (AFRC-3) or 3- and 4-cycles (AFRC-4). AFRC-3 and AFRC-4 in particular are cheaper to compute than the ORC and have been show to result in competitive rewiring methods (\cite{fesser2023mitigating}). As such, one might ask if we could not also use one of these curvature notions to compute the LCP.

